cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "cdv-phylodynamics: canine distemper virus phylodynamics in North American carnivores"
abstract: >-
  Phylodynamic analysis of canine distemper virus (Morbillivirus canis)
  hemagglutinin gene sequences from GenBank: metadata curation, alignment QC,
  maximum likelihood phylogeny, clade delineation, stratified subsampling,
  Bayesian inference with discrete host-state reconstruction, and an annotated
  Auspice dataset, applied to an America-2 lineage circulating in North
  American carnivores. The configuration, host and lineage tables, methods and
  served dataset live here; the pipeline that runs them is wildphylo, pinned by
  release tag in environment.yml. Up to v1.0.1 the pipeline was part of this
  repository. Amino acid coordinates follow the H CDS of A75/17 (AF164967).
type: software
